# Stenion database configuration.
#
# The db package (and the indexer) load the nearest .env walking up from the
# current directory, so a single .env at the repo root works for everything;
# this file documents the one variable the storage layer needs. 

# Postgres connection string. Use the *pooled* connection string from your Neon
# project dashboard (Connection Details → "Pooled connection") and paste it
# exactly as Neon gives it — Neon's string carries ?sslmode=require, and the db
# package rewrites that to sslmode=verify-full before connecting (db/src/env.ts
# explains why). Don't hand-edit the sslmode; there is nothing to configure.
# Neon's certificate is publicly valid, so verification needs no extra SSL setup.
#
# A local Postgres on localhost/127.0.0.1 is exempt from that rewrite, so the
# container flow in CONTRIBUTING.md works with no TLS at all.
#
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DBNAME?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-example-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/stenion?sslmode=require
